Consumed control source: target/bboxybook/text-raster/probe.swift.
Only the modes above were consumed; older exploratory optical PNGs were not used.
CG positioning enabled alone has no effect. Disabling CG quantization improves coverage;
rounding each shaped glyph to a quarter DEVICE pixel improves it further.
RGB context and inverse black-on-white masks do not change the result.
CG font smoothing increases the error; no stem dilation was adopted.
No separate outline-hinting switch was introduced. Integer and quarter position snaps
were measured as positioning controls, not mislabelled as an autohinter.
Exact CSS wght 500/600 replaces the measured named-face 510/590 values.
Menlo CSS 500 resolves to Regular; CG trait-only matching had selected Bold.
Logical optical size is preserved when scaling to the backing texture.

