Fractional-origin correction after the aligned probe:
The first candidate rounded a whole line to a quarter pixel before adding its glyph positions.
An eighth-pixel Chrome fixture exposed that double rounding. The final cache keeps the
full fractional line origin; the glyph is rounded only once after adding both positions.
The final 64-case fractional-origin probe has 500 changed pixels at 1x (0.047871%)
and 1768 at 2x (0.042318%). GPU and raw mask agree.
Temporary premature-rounding substitution: focused regression exit 101 (phase-red.log);
final rule exit 0 (phase-green.log). Both logs are in target/bboxybook/text-raster/.
The final quantitative matrix is galleries/release; earlier debug/phase/gamma stages remain
explicit intermediate artifacts and are not substituted for the final comparison.

